  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="38.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 38.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38.2" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ godcunde bote sece mann symle georne be boctæcinge, ⁊ woruldcunde bote sece man be woruldlage.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38.2" corresp="#wit-a">And godcunde bote sec mann symle georne be boctale, ⁊ for woruldcunde bote sece mann be weorldlage.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="38.2" corresp="#wit-q">Et Deo gratam emendationem sedulo perquiramus de scripturis sanctis et secularem iuxta legem seculi.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="38.2" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ godcunde bote sece man georne ⁊ symble be boctale, ⁊ woruldbote sece man be woruldlage.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And ecclesiastical amends shall always be diligently exacted in accordance with the directions contained in the canon law, and secular amends in accordance with secular law.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und geistliche Busse erstrebe man immer (und B) eifrig gemäss [kanonischer] Bücher-Anweisung (-Aussage B A), und (um A) weltliche Busse erstrebe man gemäss staatlichem Rechte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let spiritual atonement always be sought eagerly according to the teaching (the word, B A) of the [canonical] books, and let secular compensation be sought according to secular law.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">A's ‘for’ before ‘woruldcunde’ is Middle English.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
